-- This deck tests usage of reservoir coupling.

-- This case is a pure prediction case (no history). The master controls the production and
-- injection of the two slave models, and here also of its own wells.

-- rc_m2/masterwells: the master has a reservoir and wells of its own, and runs on two ranks.  As
-- rc_m2/t2a, but the master's grid is a 10x10x5 box at the depth of the slave RES-1 instead of one
-- cell, so that it can be split over several ranks.  It has three producers M-1H, M-2H and M-3H in
-- the group MAST_W and a water injector M-1I in the group MAST_I, in different corners of the box,
-- so that the wells end up on different ranks.  MAST_W and MAST_I are under PLAT-A, beside MOD1
-- (the master groups B1_M, D1_M, C1_M, F1_M) and the master group E1_M.  The producers use the VFP
-- table of the well B-2H of the slave RES-1 and count towards the FIELD oil target that is shared
-- with the slaves; the guide rates of the master groups decide how the target is split between
-- them and MAST_W.  M-1I is under group control: MAST_I takes the part of the water injection
-- target of 4000 Sm3/d on PLAT-A that MOD1, on a water injection limit of its own, does not
-- inject.  The master's wells start on 20 Oct 2018.  The slaves are those of rc_m2/t2a; RES-1
-- runs on three ranks.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

RUNSPEC
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DIMENS
 10 10 5 /

OIL
WATER
GAS
DISGAS
VAPOIL

METRIC

START
 1 'OCT' 2018 /


EQLDIMS
 1 1*  25 /


VFPPDIMS
--max.rate  max.THP   max.fw   max.fg   max.ALQ    max.tabs
  25        15        15       15       0          60       /


UDQDIMS
 16 16 0 5 /

UDADIMS
 5 /
